{"taskName": null, "signal": {"ticker": "MELI", "bias": "NEUTRAL", "conviction": 0.35, "rationale": "No material ticker-specific news \u2014 the items are 13F rehashes, listicles and sector commentary, which carry no weight. Technicals are the clearest input and they are soft: price below 20/50/200d SMAs, MACD negative with a deeply negative histogram, RSI 41, -4.7% over five days on thin volume (0.47x). Fundamentals are mixed: 49.8% revenue growth and 27.5% ROE against a 49x trailing P/E, high leverage (D/E 169%) and earnings down 10.9%. Analyst consensus is buy with 25% upside to target, but no fresh upgrades \u2014 that prior is already in the price, and JP Morgan/Citi sit at Neutral. Insider buying exists but is tiny and months old. Conflicting dimensions with no catalyst; earnings not until Nov 4.", "news_score": 0.0, "technical_score": -0.4, "fundamental_score": 0.15, "analyst_score": 0.3, "insider_score": 0.1, "key_factors": ["Price below 20d (-5.6%), 50d and 200d SMAs with MACD histogram -19.3", "RSI 40.8 and -4.7% over 5 days on 0.47x average volume", "Revenue +49.8% YoY but earnings -10.9%, trailing P/E 49, D/E 169%", "Consensus buy, mean target +24.7%, but no rating changes in recent weeks", "News flow is 13F filings and listicles, no ticker-specific catalyst"]}, "result": {"status": "REJECTED", "ticker": "MELI", "bias": "NEUTRAL", "conviction": 0.35, "reason": "bias is NEUTRAL; no trade", "quantity": null, "side": null, "entry_price": null, "stop_price": null, "atr": null, "order_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-09-17T15:54:52.606828Z"}, "ts": "2026-09-17 15:54:52,606", "level": "INFO", "event": "signal_processed"}
{"taskName": null, "signal": {"ticker": "SHY", "bias": "NEUTRAL", "conviction": 0.2, "rationale": "SHY is a short-government fund with 0.1% daily ATR; the front end is drifting lower as 3-month yields rose 12bp and 5-year 7bp on the week, with the dollar firmer. RSI 30.8 and price at the bottom of the 52-week range show a persistent but very low-amplitude downtrend, not a break. CFTC shows large specs net short 29.7% of open interest in 2Y notes at a 95th-percentile extreme with little weekly change -- crowded, which cuts both ways and argues against pressing a short. No rate or data surprise in the window; muni-outflow and 10y-above-5% headlines are backdrop rather than a front-end catalyst. Carry of 3.6% offsets mild price drift. Neutral.", "news_score": -0.2, "technical_score": -0.3, "fundamental_score": 0.1, "analyst_score": null, "insider_score": 0.1, "key_factors": ["3-month yield +12bp and 5-year +7bp on the week, front-end pressure", "RSI 30.8, price 4.9% up from 52-week low, 50d below 200d", "CFTC 2Y specs net short 29.7% of OI at 95th percentile -- crowded extreme", "ATR just 0.1% of price; 3.6% yield offsets modest drift", "No policy or data surprise in the window; VIX down 2.1 to 15.7"]}, "result": {"status": "REJECTED", "ticker": "SHY", "bias": "NEUTRAL", "conviction": 0.2, "reason": "bias is NEUTRAL; no trade", "quantity": null, "side": null, "entry_price": null, "stop_price": null, "atr": null, "order_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-09-17T15:57:57.707504Z"}, "ts": "2026-09-17 15:57:57,707", "level": "INFO", "event": "signal_processed"}
