{"taskName": null, "signal": {"ticker": "IWM", "bias": "NEUTRAL", "conviction": 0.2, "rationale": "A 25bp Fed hike \u2014 the first since 2023 \u2014 with a hawkish new chair and the 10-year near 5% is a genuine macro surprise, and it is unambiguously unfriendly to high-beta small caps: IWM is below its 20d and 50d SMAs, MACD negative and widening, RSI 37.7. Against that, speculative positioning is a crowded net short at the 7th percentile, which is as often the end of a move as the middle, VIX fell 2.3 on the week, the 30-year actually fell, and price bounced +0.8% on light volume. Trend is still above the 200d with 50d>200d. The bearish macro and the crowded short cancel to something close to flat; small tilt lower on momentum only. Headlines advising what levels to watch are ignored as promotional.", "news_score": -0.35, "technical_score": -0.35, "fundamental_score": 0.1, "analyst_score": 0.15, "insider_score": 0.1, "key_factors": ["FOMC raised target range 25bp to 3.75-4.00%, first hike since July 2023, unanimous", "10-year yield ~4.95%, briefly at 5%, with hawkish Fed chair commentary", "IWM below 20d (-2.4%) and 50d (-3.1%) SMAs, MACD -3.16 below signal, RSI 37.7", "CFTC large specs net short 25.5% of OI, 7th percentile of 52 weeks \u2014 crowded short", "VIX 15.56, down 2.3 on the week; bounce came on 0.75x average volume", "Analyst roll-up covers only 1.7% of fund weight \u2014 not informative about the basket"]}, "result": {"status": "REJECTED", "ticker": "IWM", "bias": "NEUTRAL", "conviction": 0.2, "reason": "bias is NEUTRAL; no trade", "quantity": null, "side": null, "entry_price": null, "stop_price": null, "atr": null, "order_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-09-17T19:03:43.119116Z"}, "ts": "2026-09-17 19:03:43,119", "level": "INFO", "event": "signal_processed"}
{"taskName": null, "signal": {"ticker": "SHY", "bias": "NEUTRAL", "conviction": 0.2, "rationale": "SHY is a 1-3yr Treasury fund; price action is a slow bleed to the bottom of its 52-week range with the front end selling off (+12bp 3m, +7bp 5y on the week), but the magnitude is tiny (ATR 0.1% of price, 1m -0.8%) and RSI 30 says the move is stretched. Credit risk is nil (99% US government, AA), yield 3.6% cushions duration loss. CFTC shows large specs net short 2Y at the 95th percentile of the year and barely changing -- a crowded short, which argues against pressing bearish. No rate or data surprise this cycle; the muni-outflow and China-yield headlines are backdrop, not a catalyst for a 2-year Treasury fund. No side worth taking.", "news_score": -0.15, "technical_score": -0.3, "fundamental_score": 0.1, "analyst_score": null, "insider_score": 0.1, "key_factors": ["Front-end yields up on the week: 3-month +12bp, 5-year +7bp; price at 81.33 near 52-week low 81.24", "RSI(14) 30.3 with ATR just 0.1% of price -- oversold but negligible volatility", "CFTC: specs net short 2Y at 95th percentile of 52 weeks, change only -0.5% of OI (crowded, stale)", "Portfolio 99.2% US government, AA 100%, yield 3.6% -- no credit risk, coupon offsets small duration loss", "Curve normal at +0.99, VIX down 2.3 to 15.6; no policy or data surprise this cycle"]}, "result": {"status": "REJECTED", "ticker": "SHY", "bias": "NEUTRAL", "conviction": 0.2, "reason": "bias is NEUTRAL; no trade", "quantity": null, "side": null, "entry_price": null, "stop_price": null, "atr": null, "order_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-09-17T19:05:47.830491Z"}, "ts": "2026-09-17 19:05:47,830", "level": "INFO", "event": "signal_processed"}
{"taskName": null, "signal": {"ticker": "TIP", "bias": "NEUTRAL", "conviction": 0.25, "rationale": "TIP sits at the bottom of its 52-week range with a 50d/200d death cross and negative MACD, consistent with rising real yields (5y 4.80%, +7bp; 3m +12bp) and a stronger dollar. The Fed resuming hikes to 3.75-4% is a genuine macro event but is already reflected in the price and in the 37% net short speculative position in 10Y notes (77th percentile), which is crowded enough to warn against pressing the short. RSI at 31.8 near the range low argues against fresh downside conviction, and the long end actually rallied (30y -6bp). Most of the newsflow is unrelated ETF listicles and market-making disclosures, which I disregard. Net: no fresh surprise large enough to justify a directional macro call, so neutral with a mild bearish tilt.", "news_score": -0.2, "technical_score": -0.4, "fundamental_score": 0.1, "analyst_score": null, "insider_score": -0.15, "key_factors": ["Price 4.5% off 52-week low; 50d SMA below 200d, MACD below signal", "Short-end yields up (3m +12bp, 5y +7bp) while 30y fell 6bp", "Fed resumed hiking, +25bp to 3.75-4%, first hike since July", "Large specs net short 37.1% of 10Y note OI, +2.0% on the week, 77th percentile crowding", "RSI 31.8 oversold, low volume 0.87x, arguing against chasing downside", "Headline flow dominated by irrelevant ETF listicles and market-making notices"]}, "result": {"status": "REJECTED", "ticker": "TIP", "bias": "NEUTRAL", "conviction": 0.25, "reason": "bias is NEUTRAL; no trade", "quantity": null, "side": null, "entry_price": null, "stop_price": null, "atr": null, "order_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-09-17T19:07:49.243480Z"}, "ts": "2026-09-17 19:07:49,243", "level": "INFO", "event": "signal_processed"}
