{"taskName": null, "signal": {"ticker": "UUP", "bias": "BULLISH", "conviction": 0.35, "rationale": "A 25bp Fed hike -- the first since 2023 -- is a genuine policy surprise and the dollar responded, with DXY +1.16 on the week to 100.25 and short-end yields leading (3m +12bp vs 10y +1bp), a hawkish front-end repricing that supports carry. UUP sits at 90% of its 52-week range, above all three moving averages with a fresh MACD cross and RSI 63, so the technical picture corroborates. Two things temper it: CFTC spec net long sits at the 93rd percentile and actually fell 3.6% on the week, so the trade is crowded and the marginal buyer may be scarce; and the move came on 0.51x average volume. Analyst roll-up covers a cash money-market holding and says nothing, so left null-ish. Modest bullish, not a heavy bet.", "news_score": 0.5, "technical_score": 0.45, "fundamental_score": 0.1, "analyst_score": 0.0, "insider_score": -0.3, "key_factors": ["Fed delivered 25bp hike, first since 2023; DXY +1.16 on week to 100.25", "3-month yield +12bp vs 10-year +1bp -- hawkish front-end repricing favours dollar carry", "Price at 90% of 52-week range, above 20/50/200d SMAs, MACD crossed positive, RSI 63", "CFTC spec net long at 93rd percentile but down 3.6% on the week -- crowded and being trimmed", "Rally occurred on 0.51x average volume; VIX down 2.3 to 15.6"]}, "result": {"status": "REJECTED", "ticker": "UUP", "bias": "BULLISH", "conviction": 0.35, "reason": "no room for broad fund UUP under its 12% cap or the sleeve budget limit: equity 99536.30, price 28.39, existing exposure 11980.58, headroom 2558.34", "quantity": null, "side": null, "entry_price": 28.389999389648438, "stop_price": 28.18, "atr": 0.10326013937637367, "order_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-09-17T19:10:55.172823Z"}, "ts": "2026-09-17 19:10:55,172", "level": "INFO", "event": "signal_processed"}
