{"taskName": null, "signal": {"ticker": "XLF", "bias": "NEUTRAL", "conviction": 0.2, "rationale": "A hawkish Fed hike with rates lifted at the short end pushed financials below their 20d and 50d SMAs; momentum is weak (RSI 38, MACD below signal) but the fund sits above a rising 200d and only 3% off highs, on light volume. Analyst roll-up on 41.5% of weight is uniformly buy with ~11% upside, and valuation is unremarkable at 16x. Rate surprise cuts both ways for banks (better margins, worse credit/deal flow), and VIX fell on the week, so nothing here supports a directional macro call. News items were mostly listicles and a promotional venue mention, which I gave no weight.", "news_score": -0.1, "technical_score": -0.3, "fundamental_score": 0.1, "analyst_score": 0.35, "insider_score": null, "key_factors": ["Fed delivered a quarter-point hike with hawkish commentary; financial stocks fell late Wednesday", "Price 2.5% below 20d and 2.1% below 50d SMA, RSI 38, MACD histogram -0.251", "Still +4.3% above 200d SMA and at 76% of 52-week range; volume only 0.64x average", "Analyst roll-up over 41.5% of fund: 100% buy, +11.1% weighted target upside", "Curve normal at +0.99, 10y flat on week, VIX down 2.3 to 15.6 \u2014 no rate regime break"]}, "result": {"status": "REJECTED", "ticker": "XLF", "bias": "NEUTRAL", "conviction": 0.2, "reason": "bias is NEUTRAL; no trade", "quantity": null, "side": null, "entry_price": null, "stop_price": null, "atr": null, "order_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-09-17T19:12:32.143981Z"}, "ts": "2026-09-17 19:12:32,144", "level": "INFO", "event": "signal_processed"}
